      "claim": "Direct human absolute/systemic availability measurements for lipophilic basic amines with two aromatic rings and propylamine-type linkers—diphenhydramine (0.69), imipramine-N-oxide (~100%), urapidil (72–78%), donepezil (~100%), laquinimod (high), oxcarbazepine (89%), tiracizine (34%), moexipril (22%), and FK788 (55%)—support F ≥ 20% for the query.",
