      "claim": "L4 intestinal absorption and permeability records for close structural analogs are strongly supportive: imipramine is essentially 100% absorbed in humans (Fa 100%), desipramine is classified as intestinally absorbed and is a high-permeability internal standard (Caco-2 Papp 82.8×10^-6 cm/s; MDCKII 38.3×10^-6 cm/s), and amitriptyline, pheniramine, and diphenhydramine show high Caco-2 permeability.",
