      "claim": "L5 gut-wall efflux records do not provide affirmative evidence for F < 20%: desipramine shows high permeability (C182); imipramine has high Papp with efflux ratio ~1.1 in classic Caco-2 and remains highly permeable even when FaSSIF gives an efflux ratio of 2.0 (C214, C178, C180, C211, C192, C195); amitriptyline shows no marked net efflux in rat intestine (C205, C190, C225, C188); methadone is a P-gp substrate yet P-gp inhibitors did not change its bioavailability (C210); dexamphetamine shows efflux ratio 1.2 (C221, C209, C217); asimadoline shows ≥20% absorption within 1 h in both wild-type and P-gp knockout mice (C203).",
