  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 gut-wall efflux and intestinal-metabolism evidence for close analogs shows high permeability and no consistent efflux-driven barrier sufficient to predict F < 20%; P-gp substrate status in methadone and high-Papp imipramine did not translate into low bioavailability. Combined with direct human F values for similar lipophilic basic amines and L4 absorption/permeability evidence, the affirmative support for F ≥ 20% remains strong. Prediction remains high; confidence remains high."
}

